 "kind": "function",
 "entry": "load_all",
 "starter": "from typing import Any, Dict, List\n\n\nclass ConfigError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised for any invalid job configuration.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass JobConfig:\n    \"\"\"Fields in order: name, board, timeout_s=600, retries=0, tags=[], env={}. Validated on construction.\"\"\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, data: Dict[str, Any]) -> \"JobConfig\":\n        pass\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        pass\n\n    def with_overrides(self, **changes) -> \"JobConfig\":\n        pass\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Provided \u2014 keep this. The tests call load_all(raws, overrides):\n#   loads each raw dict with JobConfig.from_dict, then mutates the raw input to prove you copied it;\n#   applies each [config_index, changes] override and checks the original config was left unchanged;\n#   and probes a few class-level rules (shared defaults, validation on direct construction, copies).\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List\n\n\ndef _attempt(action):\n    try:\n        return action()\n    except ConfigError as err:\n        return f\"ConfigError: {err}\"\n\n\ndef _contract():\n    a, b = JobConfig(\"a\", \"j3\"), JobConfig(\"b\", \"j3\")\n    a.tags.append(\"x\")\n    exported = a.to_dict()\n    exported[\"tags\"].append(\"y\")\n    exported[\"env\"][\"K\"] = \"V\"\n    return {\n        \"defaults_shared\": b.tags != [],\n        \"export_is_copy\": a.tags == [\"x\"] and a.env == {},\n        \"is_value_error\": isinstance(ConfigError(\"x\"), ValueError),\n        \"direct_bad_timeout\": _attempt(lambda: JobConfig(\"a\", \"j3\", timeout_s=0) and \"accepted\"),\n        \"direct_bool_retries\": _attempt(lambda: JobConfig(\"a\", \"j3\", retries=True) and \"accepted\"),\n        \"equal_by_value\": JobConfig.from_dict({\"name\": \"a\", \"board\": \"j3\"}) == JobConfig(\"a\", \"j3\"),\n    }\n\n\ndef load_all(raws: List[Dict[str, Any]], overrides: List[list]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    loaded, configs, errors = [], [], []\n    for i, raw in enumerate(raws):\n        try:\n            cfg = JobConfig.from_dict(raw)\n        except ConfigError as err:\n            errors.append(f\"{i}: {err}\")\n            continue\n        if isinstance(raw.get(\"tags\"), list):\n            raw[\"tags\"].append(\"MUTATED\")\n        if isinstance(raw.get(\"env\"), dict):\n            raw[\"env\"][\"MUTATED\"] = \"1\"\n        loaded.append(cfg)\n        configs.append(cfg.to_dict())\n    applied = []\n    for index, changes in overrides:\n        base = loaded[index]\n        before = base.to_dict()\n        result = _attempt(lambda: base.with_overrides(**changes).to_dict())\n        applied.append([result, base.to_dict() == before])\n    return {\"configs\": configs, \"errors\": errors, \"overrides\": applied, \"contract\": _contract()}\n",
 "compare": "exact",
 "notes": "Fields in order: name, board, timeout_s=600, retries=0, tags=[], env={}. Validate on every construction (including direct JobConfig(...) calls and with_overrides) in field order, raising ConfigError(\"invalid <field>\") for the first bad field: name and board are non-blank strings; timeout_s is an int from 1 to 86400 and retries an int from 0 to 5 (bool is not an int here); tags is a list of strings; env is a dict of string to string. from_dict checks, in this order: unknown keys (ConfigError(\"unknown key: <k>\") for the alphabetically first), missing name or board (ConfigError(\"missing key: <k>\"), name first), then validation. Each config owns its own lists and dicts: defaults aren't shared, from_dict copies its input, and to_dict returns copies. with_overrides(**changes) returns a new validated config and never changes the original; an unknown key gives ConfigError(\"unknown key: <k>\"). Configs compare equal by value. load_all is provided.",
